---
// A command example: a shell session, a config file, or a block of output.
//
// The body is the block's text, written with the vocabulary the stylesheet
// defines. Nothing else in a code block is coloured:
//
//   <span class="p">$ </span>   the prompt. Coloured, and never copied: the
//                               stylesheet makes it unselectable and the copy
//                               button strips it, so what lands on the
//                               clipboard is the command and not the prompt.
//   <span class="c">…</span>    a comment, muted.
//   <span class="k">…</span>    the thing to notice in the output.
//   <span class="s">…</span>    a quoted string, in a config file or a command.
//
// The Copy button is deliberately not rendered here. src/scripts/copy.ts adds
// one to every .code at runtime, so a reader with no JavaScript is never shown
// a button that cannot do anything. Keep the two in step: this component owns
// the markup, that script owns the behaviour.
const body = await Astro.slots.render('default');
// <pre> keeps whitespace, so the newlines that make the tag readable in the
// page would otherwise become a blank first and last line.
const text = body.replace(/^\r?\n|\s+$/g, '');
---

<div class="code"><pre set:html={text} /></div>
